# 1. Init Container Kya Hai?
Init Container main application container start hone se pehle run hota hai.
Pehle Init Container complete hoga.
Uske baad hi main container start hoga.
Agar Init Container fail ho gaya to Pod start nahi hoga.
> Use Case
Maan lo application ko database ready hone ke baad hi start karna hai.

Init Container
   ↓
Check Database Ready
   ↓
Main Application Start

Eample:
initContainers:
- name: wait-for-db
  image: busybox
  command: ['sh', '-c', 'until nslookup mysql; do sleep 2; done']

Kyo Use Karte Hai?
✅ Database ready hai ya nahi check karna
✅ Configuration download karna
✅ Files create karna
✅ Dependencies verify karna

Real Example
E-commerce Application:
MySQL start hone me 30 sec lag rahe hain.
Java App turant start ho jata hai aur DB connection fail ho jata hai.

Solution:
Init Container DB ready hone ka wait karega.

# 2. Sidecar Container Kya Hai?
Sidecar Container main container ke saath-saath run karta hai.
Pod jab tak chalega Sidecar bhi chalega.
> Use Case
Main application ke extra kaam Sidecar karta hai.
Main Application
       +
Sidecar Container
> Example
Application logs generate kar raha hai.

App Container
   ↓
/logs/app.log
   ↓
Sidecar Reads Logs
   ↓
Send to ELK/Splunk
> Kyo Use Karte Hai?
✅ Log collection
✅ Monitoring
✅ Security
✅ Proxy
✅ Data synchronization

